{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via an automated cobbler/orchestrator pipeline) asked me to implement srd025-unexpand requirements R3.1, R3.2, and R3.3 in the `cmd/unexpand` utility. These requirements cover custom tab stops via the `-t` flag:\n   - **R3.1**: `-t N` sets a uniform tab stop interval of N columns. `-t LIST` sets absolute tab stop positions. Behavior mirrors srd024-expand R2.1 and R2.2.\n   - **R3.2**: When past the last explicit tab stop in a LIST, remaining spaces are kept as-is (no tab can be inserted beyond the last defined stop).\n   - **R3.3**: `-t` implies `-a`; when custom tab stops are given, all whitespace in the line is subject to conversion, not just leading whitespace.\n   \n   The task requires modifying `cmd/unexpand/main.go` and `cmd/unexpand/unexpand_test.go`, then verifying with `go build`, `go vet`, and `go test`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GNU `unexpand` reimplementation in Go with differential testing against `gunexpand` (Homebrew)\n   - Tab stop resolution: uniform interval (`-t N`) vs explicit positions list (`-t LIST`)\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` differential testing framework comparing Go binary vs GNU reference binary\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - `LC_ALL=C` for deterministic locale behavior in tests\n   - The cobbler-scaffold pipeline manages git — no git commands allowed\n   - Execution constitution mandates: 40-line function limit, copyright headers, write-first strategy (write all code then build once)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **`docs/specs/software-requirements/srd025-unexpand.yaml`** (READ)\n     - Full SRD defining all requirements R1-R4. R3 section (lines 41-48) defines the custom tab stops behavior needed.\n     - Key: R3.2 says \"When past the last explicit tab stop in a LIST, remaining spaces are kept as-is (no tab can be inserted beyond the last defined stop).\"\n     - Key: R3.3 says \"-t implies -a\"\n\n   - **`cmd/unexpand/main.go`** (READ, needs MODIFICATION)\n     - Already implements R1.1-R1.4 (default leading-only) and R2.1-R2.3 (-a all mode)\n     - `parseArgs` (line 56-98): Already parses `-t` flag and sets `allMode = true` (R3.3 partially done)\n     - `parseTabStops` (line 100-126): Already parses single interval and comma-separated list\n     - `nextTabStop` (line 194-205): Returns next tab stop column. **BUG for R3.2**: When past all explicit positions, returns `col + 1` which causes `emitCompacted` to emit tabs for single-column advances instead of keeping spaces\n     - `emitCompacted` (line 207-220): Compacts space runs into tabs. **Needs fix for R3.2**: Must not emit tabs when past the last explicit tab stop in a list\n     - `unexpand` (line 128-192): Main processing loop. Tab handling in this function also needs to account for R3.2 (no tab advancement past last stop)\n     \n     Critical code - `nextTabStop`:\n     ```go\n     func nextTabStop(col int, stops tabStops) int {\n         if stops.positions == nil {\n             return col + stops.interval - (col-1)%stops.interval\n         }\n         colIdx := col - 1\n         for _, p := range stops.positions {\n             if p > colIdx {\n                 return p + 1\n             }\n         }\n         return col + 1  // BUG: This causes tabs to be emitted past last stop\n     }\n     ```\n     \n     Critical code - `emitCompacted`:\n     ```go\n     func emitCompacted(w *bufio.Writer, startCol int, count int, stops tabStops) {\n         col := startCol\n         end := startCol + count\n         for col < end {\n             next := nextTabStop(col, stops)\n             if next <= end {\n                 w.WriteByte('\\t')\n                 col = next\n             } else {\n                 w.WriteByte(' ')\n                 col++\n             }\n         }\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **`cmd/unexpand/unexpand_test.go`** (READ, needs MODIFICATION)\n     - Has tests for R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.3 but NO tests for R3.x (custom tab stops)\n     - Uses differential testing pattern with `testutils.BuildBinary` and `testutils.RunDiffTests`\n     - Reference binary: `gunexpand` via `exec.LookPath`\n     - Need to add test cases for `-t N` (uniform interval), `-t LIST` (explicit positions), behavior past last stop (R3.2), and `-t` implying `-a` (R3.3)\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet — I had just finished reading the three files and was about to begin implementation when the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **Identified the R3.2 bug**: The current `nextTabStop` returns `col + 1` when past all explicit positions in a list. This makes `emitCompacted` write tab characters for single-column advances, which is incorrect. GNU unexpand keeps spaces as-is when past the last defined tab stop.\n   - **Solution approach**: Need to either:\n     (a) Have `nextTabStop` return a sentinel value (e.g., 0 or -1) when past all stops, and have `emitCompacted` check for it, OR\n     (b) Add a helper function `pastLastStop(col, stops)` that `emitCompacted` checks before emitting a tab, OR\n     (c) Modify `emitCompacted` to check if `stops.positions != nil` and the current column is past the last position, in which case just emit spaces\n   - R3.1 appears already implemented (parsing works for both `-t N` and `-t LIST`)\n   - R3.3 appears already implemented (`allMode = true` in `parseArgs` when `-t` is used)\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Extremely long task specification providing the full project context, SRD, architecture, execution constitution, go style guide, task description requiring implementation of srd025-unexpand R3.1-R3.3 with specific files to modify, requirements, design decisions, and acceptance criteria.\n   -