mplexity with the nested structure. Let me simplify by checking if we're past the last stop directly within the main loop, using a tab when possible and falling back to spaces otherwise. This keeps everything clean and avoids extra helper functions.\n\nNow I'm thinking through how tab characters in the input interact with the `unexpand` logic when we're already past the last defined stop—there's a subtlety around how `nextTabStop` should behave in that case. I'm realizing the double-counting issue: when spaces accumulate, `col` already reflects their position, so adding `spaceRun` again to calculate the next tab stop is incorrect. The actual column where the tab should land is just `col`, not `col+spaceRun`.\n\nSince there's no test covering spaces-then-tab, this bug went undetected, but fixing it is out of scope for this task. I'll stick to implementing R3.2: emitting spaces in `emitCompacted` when we're past the last explicit stop, and leave the tab handling as-is.\n\nNow I'm writing the code changes—adding a helper function to check if we're past the last stop, then modifying `emitCompacted` to handle that case.\n\nFinishing the implementation...\n\nFor the tests, I need to add cases with the `-t` flag to verify both uniform intervals and explicit tab stop positions work correctly, including edge cases like spaces that don't reach a stop.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15474,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15474},"output_tokens":38,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d732b864-6463-4f63-a0ba-0415efc70679","uuid":"8a71b5c1-1a2a-4515-ab42-048a5de7f9af"}
